---
// A horizontal static-firing stand, schematic: the thrust path from the motor through the load cell to the thrust
// block, the flexures that let the motor move along its axis, the in-place calibration, and the main measurements.
const ink = 'var(--rd-ink)', muted = 'var(--rd-muted)', steel = 'var(--rd-steel)', blue = 'var(--rd-blue)', hot = 'var(--rd-hot)';
const cy = 114, r = 30; // motor axis and radius
---

<figure class="viz test-stand">
  <p class="viz-title">A horizontal thrust stand</p>
  <svg viewBox="0 0 440 240" role="img" aria-labelledby="ts-desc" style="max-width: 640px; margin: 0 auto;">
    <desc id="ts-desc">
      A motor lies horizontally in cradles on a mount. Thin vertical flexures hold the mount to the ground: they are
      stiff sideways and soft along the axis, so the motor can push forward. The thrust goes from the forward end of the
      motor through a thrust adapter and a load cell into a thrust block. Below the load cell, a hydraulic actuator and
      a reference load cell can push on the mount to calibrate the whole thrust path in place. Pressure transducers are
      at the forward closure, and thermocouples and strain gauges are on the case. The aft cradle lets the case grow
      along its length.
    </desc>
    <defs>
      <pattern id="ts-hatch" width="6" height="6" patternUnits="userSpaceOnUse" patternTransform="rotate(45)">
        <line x1="0" y1="0" x2="0" y2="6" stroke="var(--rd-line)" stroke-width="2"></line>
      </pattern>
    </defs>
    <!-- ground and thrust block -->
    <rect x="8" y="200" width="424" height="8" fill="url(#ts-hatch)"></rect>
    <line x1="8" x2="432" y1="200" y2="200" stroke={muted}></line>
    <rect x="14" y="70" width="40" height="130" fill={muted} fill-opacity="0.35" stroke={muted}></rect>
    <!-- load cell and thrust adapter -->
    <rect x="54" y={cy - 9} width="20" height="18" rx="3" fill={steel} stroke={ink} stroke-width="0.8"></rect>
    <rect x="74" y={cy - 24} width="10" height="48" fill={steel}></rect>
    <!-- motor -->
    <rect x="84" y={cy - r} width="246" height={2 * r} rx="22" fill={blue} fill-opacity="0.35" stroke={blue}></rect>
    <path d={`M330,${cy - 10} L372,${cy - 26} L372,${cy + 26} L330,${cy + 10} Z`} fill={steel} stroke={ink} stroke-width="0.8"></path>
    <path d={`M372,${cy - 24} Q404,${cy - 18} 430,${cy} Q404,${cy + 18} 372,${cy + 24} Z`} fill={hot} fill-opacity="0.45"></path>
    <!-- mount, cradles and flexures -->
    <rect x="110" y="150" width="200" height="10" fill={steel}></rect>
    <path d={`M136,150 L136,${cy + r - 2} Q150,${cy + r + 6} 164,${cy + r - 2} L164,150 Z M262,150 L262,${cy + r - 2} Q276,${cy + r + 6} 290,${cy + r - 2} L290,150 Z`} fill={steel}></path>
    <rect x="126" y="160" width="4" height="40" fill={ink}></rect>
    <rect x="290" y="160" width="4" height="40" fill={ink}></rect>
    <!-- calibration: actuator and reference load cell, pushing on the mount -->
    <rect x="54" y="168" width="30" height="12" fill={muted} fill-opacity="0.8"></rect>
    <rect x="84" y="170" width="12" height="8" rx="2" fill={steel} stroke={ink} stroke-width="0.6"></rect>
    <line x1="96" x2="110" y1="174" y2="158" stroke={ink} stroke-width="2"></line>
    <!-- instrumentation -->
    <circle cx="96" cy={cy - 16} r="3.5" fill="var(--rd-accent)"></circle>
    {[150, 210, 250].map((x) => <circle cx={x} cy={cy - r} r="2.6" fill={ink}></circle>)}
    <!-- the thrust arrow -->
    <path d={`M200,${cy} L120,${cy} M128,${cy - 5} L120,${cy} L128,${cy + 5}`} fill="none" stroke={ink} stroke-width="1.6"></path>
    <text x="210" y={cy + 4} font-size="10.5" fill={ink}>thrust</text>
    <!-- labels -->
    <text transform="translate(38,136) rotate(-90)" font-size="10" fill={ink} text-anchor="middle">thrust block</text>
    <line x1="64" x2="64" y1="40" y2={cy - 10} stroke={muted}></line>
    <text x="64" y="34" font-size="10.5" fill={ink} text-anchor="middle">load cell</text>
    <line x1="97" x2="140" y1={cy - 20} y2="50" stroke={muted}></line>
    <text x="142" y="48" font-size="10.5" fill={ink}>pressure transducers</text>
    <line x1="210" x2="236" y1={cy - r - 3} y2="72" stroke={muted}></line>
    <text x="238" y="70" font-size="10.5" fill={ink}>thermocouples, strain gauges</text>
    <line x1="290" x2="324" y1={cy + r + 4} y2="170" stroke={muted}></line>
    <text x="326" y="174" font-size="10" fill={muted}>aft cradle slides:</text>
    <text x="326" y="187" font-size="10" fill={muted}>the case grows</text>
    <line x1="128" x2="160" y1="190" y2="218" stroke={muted}></line>
    <text x="162" y="222" font-size="10" fill={muted}>flexures: stiff sideways, soft along the axis</text>
    <line x1="70" x2="70" y1="180" y2="226" stroke={muted}></line>
    <text x="74" y="236" font-size="10" fill={muted}>in-place calibration</text>
  </svg>
  <figcaption>
    The thrust path is the measurement: everything between the motor and the load cell (adapter, flexures, cables and
    pipes) shares the force. Thus the calibration pushes through the same path, in place, before and after the firing.
    The motor must move freely along its axis onto the load cell, and the aft cradle must let the case grow.
  </figcaption>
</figure>
